{
  "title": "Namaz of Imam Ali (a.s.)",
  "data": "Pray 4 units. In each unit, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) 50 times.\nAfter the prayer, recite this litany of Imam Ali (a.s.):\nسُبْحَانَ مَنْ لَا تَبِيْدُ مَعَالِمُهٗ\nSUBHAANA MAN LAA TABEEDU MA'AALIMUH\nGlory be to Him Whose signs never perish.\nسُبْحَانَ مَنْ لَا تَنْقُصُ خَزَاۤئِنُهٗ\nSUBHAANA MAN LAA TANQUSU KHAZAA'INUH\nGlory be to Him Whose reserves never downgrade.\nسُبْحَانَ مَنْ لَا اضْمِحْلَالَ لِفَخْرِهٖ\nSUBHAANA MAN LAD MIHLAALA LIFAKHRIH\nGlory be to Him Whose honor never vanishes.\nسُبْحَانَ مَنْ لَا يَنْفَدُ مَا عِنْدَهٗ\nSUBHAANA MAN LAA YANFADU MAA I'NDAH\nGlory be to Him Whose possessions never run out.\nسُبْحَانَ مَنْ لَا انْقِطَاعَ لِمُدَّتِهٖ\nSUBHAANA MAN LAN QITAA'A LIMUDDATIH\nGlory be to Him Whose duration (of existence) is never interrupted.\nسُبْحَانَ مَنْ لَا يُشَارِكُ اَحَدًا فِي اَمْرِهٖ\nSUBHAANA MAN LAA YUSHAARIKU AHADAN FEE AMRIH\nGlory be to Him Who never betakes to Himself a partner in His affairs.\nسُبْحَانَ مَنْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ غَيْرُهُ\nSUBHAANA MAN LAA ILAAHA GHAYRUH\nGlory be to Him save Whom there is no god.\nThen recite this supplication:\nيَا مَنْ عَفَا عَنِ السَّيِّئَاتِ وَلَمْ يُجَازِ بِهَا\nYAA MAN A'FAA A'NIS SAYYI'AATI WA LAM YUJAAZI BIHAA\nO He who overlooks sins and does not inflict punishment in return,\nاِرْحَمْ عَبْدَكَ يَا اَللهُ نَفْسِيْ نَفْسِيْ\nIRHAM A'BDAKA YAA ALLAAHU NAFSEE NAFSEE\n(please) have mercy on Your servant, O Allah, that is I myself, that is I myself.\nاَنَا عَبْدُكَ يَا سَيِّدَاهُ اَنَا عَبْدُكَ بَيْنَ يَدَيْكَ اَيَا رَبَّاهُ\nANAA A'BDUKA YAA SAYYIDAAHU ANAA A'BDUKA BAYNA YADAYKA AYAA RABBAAH\nI am Your servant, O my Chief, I am Your servant; I am at Your disposal; O my Lord.\nاِلٰهِيْ بِكَيْنُوْنَتِكَ يَا اَمَلَاهُ يَا رَحْمَانَاهُ يَا غِيَاثَاهُ عَبْدُكَ عَبْدُكَ لَا حِيْلَةَ لَهٗ\nILAAHEE BIKAYNOONATIKA YAA AMALAAHU YAA RAHMAANAAHU YAA GHIYAATHAAHU A'BDUKA A'BDUKA LAA HEELATA LAH\nO my God, in the name of Your Being, O my Hope, O my All-beneficent, O my Supporter, Your servant, Your servant, has no strategy.\nيَا مُنْتَهٰى رَغْبَتَاهُ\nYAA MUNTAHAA RAGHBATAAH\nO Ultimate of my desire!\nيَا مُجْرِيَ الدَّمِ فِي عُرُوْقِي [عَبْدُكَ]\nYAA MUJRIYAD DAMI FEE U'ROOQEE [A'BDUK]\nO He Who makes blood run into the veins of Your slave!\nيَا سَيِّدَاهُ يَا مَالِكَاهُ اَيَا هُوَ اَيَا هُوَ يَا رَبَّاهُ\nYAA SAYYIDAAHU YAA MAALIKAAHU AYAA HUWA AYAA HUWA YAA RABBAAH\nO my Chief, O my Master! O He Who is Unique! O He Who is Unique! O my Lord!\nعَبْدُكَ عَبْدُكَ لَا حِيْلَةَ لِيْ وَلَا غِنٰى بِيْ عَنْ نَفْسِيْ\nA'BDUKA A'BDUKA LAA HEELATA LEE WA LAA GHINAA BEE A'N NAFSEE\nI - Your servant, Your servant - have no strategy and I cannot avail myself\nوَلَا اَسْتَطِيْعُ لَهَا ضَرًّا وَلَا نَفْعًا\nWA LAA ASTATEE'U LAHAA DARRAN WA LAA NAF'AA\nand I have no control over loss or over profit.\nوَلَا اَجِدُ مَنْ اُصَانِعُهٗ\nWA LAA AJIDU MAN USAANI'UH\nI do not find anyone from whom I may seek help;\nتَقَطَّعَتْ اَسْبَابُ الْخَدَاۤئِعِ عَنِّي\nTAQATTA'AT ASBAABUL KHADAA'I'I A'NNEE\nso, all profitable avenues have been blocked,\nوَاضْمَحَلَّ كُلُّ مَظْنُوْنٍ عَنِّي\nWADMAHALLA KULLU MAZNOONIN A'NNEE\nand all my expectations have turned into disappointments.\nاَفْرَدَنِي الدَّهْرُ اِلَيْكَ\nAFRADANID DAHRU ILAYK\nHelpless and forsaken I came to You,\nفَقُمْتُ بَيْنَ يَدَيْكَ هٰذَا الْمَقَامَ\nFAQUMTU BAYNA YADAYKA HAADHAL MAQAAM\nSo, I have presented myself before You in this current stand.\nيَا اِلٰهِيْ بِعِلْمِكَ كَانَ هٰذَا كُلُّهٗ\nYAA ILAAHEE BI-I'LMIKA KAANA HAADHAA KULLUH\nO my God, You are aware of all that which I speak about.\nفَكَيْفَ اَنْتَ صَانِعٌ بِيْ\nFAKAYFA ANTA SAANI'UN BEE\nSo, how would You deal with me?\nوَلَيْتَ شِعْرِيْ كَيْفَ تَقُوْلُ لِدُعَاۤئِي\nWALAYTA SHI'REE KAYFA TAQOOLU LIDU'AA'EE\nIf I but knew how would You dispense with my prayer?\nاَ تَقُوْلُ نَعَمْ اَمْ تَقُوْلُ لَا\nA TAQOOLU NA'AM AM TAQOOLU LAA\nWould You say, ‘Yes’ or ‘No’?\nفَاِنْ قُلْتَ لَا فَيَا وَيْلِيْ يَا وَيْلِيْ يَا وَيْلِيْ\nFA-IN QULTA LAA FAYAA WAYLEE YAA WAYLEE YAA WAYLEE\nIf You say ‘No,’ then I am ruined! I am ruined! I am ruined!\nيَا عَوْلِيْ يَا عَوْلِيْ يَا عَوْلِيْ\nYAA A'WLEE YAA A'WLEE YAA A'WLEE\nWoe to me! Woe to me! Woe to me!\nيَا شِقْوَتِيْ يَا شِقْوَتِيْ يَا شِقْوَتِيْ\nYAA SHIQWATEE YAA SHIQWATEE YAA SHIQWATEE\nOh my misery! Oh my misery! Oh my misery!\nيَا ذُلِّيْ يَا ذُلِّيْ يَا ذُلِّيْ\nYAA DHULLEE YAA DHULLEE YAA DHULLEE\nOh my ill-luck! Oh my ill-luck! Oh my ill-luck!\nاِلٰى مَنْ وَمِمَّنْ اَوْ عِنْدَ مَنْ اَوْ كَيْفَ اَوْ مَا ذَا اَوْ اِلٰى اَيِّ شَيْءٍ اَلْجَاُ\nILAA MAN WA MIMMAN AW I'NDA MAN AW KAYFA AW MAA DHAA AW ILAA AYYI SHAY'IN ALJA'\nTo whom? By Whom? From whom? How? What? In which place to take shelter?\nوَمَنْ اَرْجُوْ\nWA MAN ARJOO\nFor whom shall I hope?\nوَمَنْ يَجُوْدُ عَلَيَّ بِفَضْلِهٖ حِيْنَ تَرْفُضُنِيْ\nWA MAN YAJOODU A'LAYYA BIFADLIHEE HEENA TARFUDUNEE\nWho shall bestow upon me with his favor when You forsake me?\nيَا وَاسِعَ الْمَغْفِرَةِ\nYAA WAASI'AL MAGHFIRAH\nO Liberal in forgiveness!\nوَاِنْ قُلْتَ نَعَمْ كَمَا هُوَ الظَّنُّ بِكَ وَالرَّجَاۤءُ لَكَ\nWA IN QULTA NA'AM KAMAA HUWAZ ZANNU BIKA WAR RAJAA'U LAK\nBut if You say ‘Yes,’ as I expect You to say and as I desire from You,\nفَطُوْبٰى لِيْ اَنَا السَّعِيْدُ وَاَنَا الْمَسْعُوْدُ فَطُوْبٰى لِيْ وَاَنَا الْمَرْحُوْمُ\nFATOOBAA LEE ANAS SA'EEDU WA ANAL MAS'OODU FATOOBAA LEE WA ANAL MARHOOM\nthen joy is for me, I am successful, I am happy; then joy is for me, I will receive (Your) mercy.\nيَا مُتَرَحِّمُ يَا مُتَرَئِّفُ يَا مُتَعَطِّفُ يَا مُتَجَبِّرُ [مُتَحَنِّنُ] يَا مُتَمَلِّكُ يَا مُقْسِطُ\nYAA MUTARAHHIMU YAA MUTARA''IFU YAA MUTA'ATTIFU YAA MUTAJABBIRU [MUTAHANNINU] YAA MUTAMALLIKU YAA MUQSIT\nO Ever-merciful! O Ever-compassionate! O Ever-sympathetic! O Ever-commiserating! O Ever-sovereign! O Just!\nلَا عَمَلَ لِيْ اَبْلُغُ بِهٖ نَجَاحَ حَاجَتِيْ\nLAA A'MALA LEE ABLUGHU BIHEE NAJAAHA HAAJATEE\nI lack any act due to which I can attain achievement of my desire.\nاَسْاَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ الَّذِيْ جَعَلْتَهٗ فِي مَكْنُوْنِ غَيْبِكَ وَاسْتَقَرَّ عِنْدَكَ فَلَا يَخْرُجُ مِنْكَ اِلٰى شَيْءٍ سِوَاكَ\nAS'ALUKA BISMIKAL LADHEE JA'ALTAHOO FEE MAKNOONI GHAYBIKA WASTAQARRA I'NDAKA FALAA YAKHRUJU MINKA ILAA SHAY'IN SIWAAK\nI thus beseech You in the name of Your Name which You have reserved in the innermost of Your Hidden Knowledge and it has thus settled with You so firmly that nothing of it can come out from You to any other thing.\nاَسْاَلُكَ بِهٖ وَبِكَ وَبِهٖ فَاِنَّهٗ اَجَلُّ وَاَشْرَفُ اَسْمَاۤئِكَ\nAS'ALUKA BIHEE WA BIKA WA BIHEE FA-INNAHOO AJALLU WA ASHRAFU ASMAA'IK\nI beseech You by it and by You, for it is certainly the most exalted and honored of Your Names.\nلَا شَيْءً لِيْ غَيْرُ هٰذَا وَلَا اَحَدَ اَعْوَدُ عَلَيَّ مِنْكَ\nLAA SHAY'AN LEE GHAYRU HAADHAA WA LAA AHADA A'WADU A'LAYYA MINK\nI have nothing to mention except this, and no one can be more beneficent to me than You.\nيَا كَيْنُوْنُ يَا مُكَوِّنُ\nYAA KAYNOONU YAA MUKAWWIN\nO Absolute Being! O Creator of creation!\nيَا مَنْ عَرَّفَنِيْ نَفْسَهٗ يَا مَنْ اَمَرَنِيْ بِطَاعَتِهٖ يَا مَنْ نَهَانِيْ عَنْ مَعْصِيَتِهٖ\nYAA MAN A'RRAFANEE NAFSAHOO YAA MAN AMARANEE BITAA'ATIHEE YAA MAN NAHAANEE A'N MA'SIYATIH\nO He Who has introduced Himself to me! O He Who has commanded me to obey Him! O He Who has warned me against disobeying Him!\nوَيَا مَدْعُوُّ يَا مَسْئُوْلُ يَا مَطْلُوْبًا اِلَيْهِ\nWA YAA MAD'UWWU YAA MAS'OOLU YAA MATLOOBAN ILAYH\nO He Who is besought! O He Who is pleaded! O He Who is desired!\nرَفَضْتُ وَصِيَّتَكَ الَّتِيْ اَوْصَيْتَنِيْ وَلَمْ اُطِعْكَ\nRAFADTU WASIYYATAKAL LATEE AWSAYTANEE WA LAM UTI'K\nI have overlooked Your instructions, which You gave me and have not obeyed You.\nوَلَوْ اَطَعْتُكَ فِيْمَا اَمَرْتَنِيْ لَكَفَيْتَنِيْ مَا قُمْتُ اِلَيْكَ فِيْهِ\nWA LAW ATA'TUKA FEEMAA AMARTANEE LAKAFAYTANEE MAA QUMTU ILAYKA FEEH\nIf I obeyed You in what You have ordered me, You would certainly grant my requests that I am presenting before You.\nوَاَنَا مَعَ مَعْصِيَّتِيْ لَكَ رَاجٍ\nWA ANAA MA'A MA'SIYYATEE LAKA RAAJ\nIn spite of my transgression, I am hopeful for You.\nفَلَا تَحُلْ بَيْنِيْ وَبَيْنَ مَا رَجَوْتُ\nFALAA TAHUL BAYNEE WA BAYNA MAA RAJAWT\nSo, do not let my hope remain unfulfilled.\nيَا مُتَرَحِّمًا لِيْ اَعِذْنِيْ مِنْ بَيْنِ يَدَيَّ وَمِنْ خَلْفِيْ وَمِنْ فَوْقِي وَمِنْ تَحْتِي وَمِنْ كُلِّ جِهَاتِ الْاِحَاطَةِ بِيْ\nYAA MUTARAHHIMAN LEE A'IDHNEE MIN BAYNI YADAYYA WA MIN KHALFEE WA MIN FAWQEE WA MIN TAHTEE WA MIN KULLI JIHAATIL IHAATATI BEE\nO He Who always has mercy upon me, keep me safe, under Your protection, from (all evils that are) before me, behind me, above me, below me, and from all sides that surround me.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ بِمُحَمَّدٍ سَيِّدِيْ وَبِعَلِيٍّ وَلِيِّيْ وَبِالْاَئِمَّةِ الرَّاشِدِيْنَ عَلَيْهِمُ السَّلَامُ\nALLAAHUMMA BIMUHAMMADIN SAYYIDEE WA BI-A'LIYYIN WALIYYEE WA BIL A'IMMATIR RAASHIDEENA A'LAYHIMUS SALAAM\nO Allah, [I beseech You] in the name of Muhammad, my master, and [in the name of] 'Ali, my chief, and [in the names of] the orthodox Imams (leaders), peace be upon them,\nاِجْعَلْ عَلَيْنَا صَلَوَاتِكَ وَرَاْفَتَكَ وَرَحْمَتَكَ\nIJ'AL A'LAYNAA SALAWAATIKA WA RA'FATAKA WA RAHMATAK\n(please) bestow upon us with Your blessings, compassions, and mercy;\nوَاَوْسِعْ عَلَيْنَا مِنْ رِّزْقِكَ وَاقْضِ عَنَّا الدَّيْنَ وَجَمِيْعَ حَوَاۤئِجِنَا\nWA AWSI' A'LAYNAA MIR RIZQIKA WAQDI A'NNAD DAYNA WA JAMEE'A HAWAA'IJINAA\nand grant us expansive shares of Your sustenance; and help us repay our debts and settle all our needs,\nيَا اَللهُ يَا اَللهُ يَا اَللهُ\nYAA ALLAAHU YAA ALLAAHU YAA ALLAAH\nO Allah, O Allah, O Allah.\nاِنَّكَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ\nINNAKA A'LAA KULLI SHAY'IN QADEER\nVerily, You have full power over all things.\nAfter this prayer, also recite:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى النَّبِيِّ الْعَرَبِيِّ وَاٰلِهِ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAN NABIYYIL A'RABIYYI WA AALIH\nO Allah, send blessings to the Arab Prophet and on his Household.",
  "merits": "Shaykh al-Tusi and Sayyid Ibn Tawus have recorded that Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a.s.) said: One who offers the four-unit prayer of Imam Ali Amir al-Mu'minin (a.s.) will be as free of sins as newborns and will have all his requests granted.\n\nThe Imam (a.s.) then added: One who offers this prayer and says this supplication will have all his sins forgiven.\n\nNumerous are the narrations that have mentioned splendid reward for those who offer this prayer on Fridays. Similarly, one who says the salawat on the Arab Prophet after that prayer will have all his previous and coming sins forgiven, will be given the reward of him who recites the holy Qur'an entirely twelve times, and will be saved from thirst on the Resurrection Day."
}
